/*  Text — `the length of`, `the characters from … to … of`, `contains`, `starts with`, `ends with`,
    `the position of … in`, `replace … with … in`, `trimmed`, `split by`, `in uppercase` and `in
    lowercase`, `the first … characters of` and `the last … characters of`, `the current directory`, and `the environment variable`.

    ★ Each is the runtime's own call, the one `cufet build` makes, so a text is measured and cut in
      CHARACTERS — code points — and never in bytes.

    ★ `in uppercase` and `in lowercase` read the case table in the shared runtime, which the
      interpreter's table generates — so both agree by construction.
*/

Pull a book on collections.
    /// Whether an expression is one of the text operations here.
    Bind fact to is-text-operation, given (the text kind):
        Return kind is "TextSubstringRange" or kind is "TextContains" or kind is "TextAffixTest" or kind is "TextFind"
            or kind is "TextReplace" or kind is "TextTrim" or kind is "TextSplit" or kind is "NumberConvert"
            or kind is "TextCase" or kind is "TextSubstringEdge" or kind is "CurrentDirectoryExpression"
            or kind is "PathCheckExpression" or kind is "EnvironmentVariableExpression".
    Done.

    Bind text to text-operation-kind, given (the text kind):
        If kind is "TextContains" or kind is "TextAffixTest" or kind is "PathCheckExpression", return "fact".
        If kind is "TextFind" or kind is "NumberConvert", return "voidable number".
        If kind is "CurrentDirectoryExpression" or kind is "EnvironmentVariableExpression", return "voidable text".
        If kind is "TextSplit", return "series of text".
        Return "text".
    Done.

    /// A text operation as C.
    Bind text or failure to c-text-operation unto emitter, given (the node expression):
        Define kind as expression's kind.
        If kind is "TextFind":
            Define found as cast one's c-fields-in-order on (expression, 1, 2) or pass the failure off.
            Return cast in-order on (item 1 of found, "(\{ int cf_fd = cufet_str_find({item 3 of found}, {item 2 of found}); cf_fd ? cvo_number_some(cufet_dec_from_ll(cf_fd)) : cvo_number_none(); \})").
        Done.
        // `the current directory` — void when there is none to report.
        If kind is "CurrentDirectoryExpression":
            Return "(\{ const char* cf_cwd = cufet_getcwd(); cf_cwd ? cvo_text_some(cf_cwd) : cvo_text_none(); \})".
        Done.
        // Those with more than one operand, each worked out in turn.
        If kind is "TextSubstringEdge" or kind is "TextContains" or kind is "TextAffixTest" or kind is "TextSplit"
                or kind is "TextReplace" or kind is "TextSubstringRange":
            Return cast one's c-text-of-several on (expression) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        Define text-c as cast one's c-of on (cast field-of on (expression, 1)) or pass the failure off.
        If kind is "TextTrim", return "cufet_str_trim({text-c})".
        // `the environment variable <name>` — void when it is not set.
        If kind is "EnvironmentVariableExpression":
            Return "(\{ const char* cf_ev = cufet_getenv({text-c}); cf_ev ? cvo_text_some(cf_ev) : cvo_text_none(); \})".
        Done.
        // `the path … exists`, `is a directory`, `is a file`.
        If kind is "PathCheckExpression":
            Define asked as (cast field-of on (expression, 2))'s word.
            If asked is "Exists", return "cufet_path_exists({text-c})".
            If asked is "IsDirectory", return "cufet_path_is_dir({text-c})".
            If asked is "IsFile", return "cufet_path_is_file({text-c})".
            Return a failure (cast not-built on ("the path check {asked}")).
        Done.
        // Casing reads the shared runtime's table — the one the interpreter reads too.
        If kind is "TextCase":
            If (cast field-of on (expression, 2))'s word is "true", return "cufet_str_upper({text-c})".
            Return "cufet_str_lower({text-c})".
        Done.
        // `converted to number` — of a text; void when it is no number.
        If kind is "NumberConvert":
            If (cast one's kind-of on (cast field-of on (expression, 1)) or pass the failure off) is "bits":
                Return "cufet_bits_to_number({text-c})".
            Done.
            Return "(\{ CufetDec cf_pn; cufet_parse_number({text-c}, &cf_pn) ? cvo_number_some(cf_pn) : cvo_number_none(); \})".
        Done.
        Return a failure (cast not-built on (kind)).
    Done.

    /// A text operation of two or three operands as C, the operands worked out in turn.
    Bind text or failure to c-text-of-several unto emitter, given (the node expression):
        Define kind as expression's kind.
        Define last as 2.
        If kind is "TextReplace", the last becomes 3.
        If kind is "TextSubstringRange" and cast is-nothing on (cast field-of on (expression, 3)) is false, the last becomes 3.
        Define sides as cast one's c-fields-in-order on (expression, 1, last) or pass the failure off.
        Define prefix as item 1 of sides.
        Define text-c as item 2 of sides.
        Define second as item 3 of sides.
        // `the first <n> characters of`, `the last <n> characters of` — as many as there are.
        If kind is "TextSubstringEdge":
            If (cast field-of on (expression, 3))'s word is "true", return cast in-order on (prefix, "cufet_str_edge({text-c}, cufet_to_int({second}), 1)").
            Return cast in-order on (prefix, "cufet_str_edge({text-c}, cufet_to_int({second}), 0)").
        Done.
        If kind is "TextContains", return cast in-order on (prefix, "(strstr({text-c}, {second}) != NULL)").
        If kind is "TextAffixTest":
            If (cast field-of on (expression, 3))'s word is "true", return cast in-order on (prefix, "cufet_str_ends({text-c}, {second})").
            Return cast in-order on (prefix, "cufet_str_starts({text-c}, {second})").
        Done.
        If kind is "TextSplit":
            Return cast in-order on (prefix, "(\{ cser_text* cf_sp = cser_text_new(); const char** cf_parts; int cf_n = cufet_str_split({text-c}, {second}, &cf_parts, {(cast field-of on (expression, 3))'s word}); for (int cf_j = 0; cf_j < cf_n; cf_j++) cser_text_append(cf_sp, cf_parts[cf_j]); cf_sp; \})").
        Done.
        If kind is "TextReplace":
            Return cast in-order on (prefix, "cufet_str_replace({text-c}, {second}, {item 4 of sides}, {(cast field-of on (expression, 4))'s word})").
        Done.
        // `the characters from … to … of`, to the end when there is no `to`.
        Define upto as "-1".
        If last is 3, the upto becomes "cufet_to_int({item 4 of sides})".
        Return cast in-order on (prefix, "cufet_str_range({text-c}, cufet_to_int({second}), {upto}, {(cast field-of on (expression, 4))'s word})").
    Done.

    /// `the length of <text>` — in characters.
    Bind text to c-text-length, given (the text text-c):
        Return "cufet_dec_from_ll((long long)cufet_u8_len({text-c}))".
    Done.
Done.
